      "bot": false,
      "body": "**Addendum (owner directive, live-test follow-up): `3bc3d30d35` — unanswered inbound agent mail is never a compaction candidate.\n\n**Trigger.** A live clip from a DAP multi-agent session: a peer's mail delivered into a busy agent, the autonomous chain then paused on its budget with one message queued — while earlier delivered-but-unanswered mail was foldable by every mechanical tier. The prompt-level belt (`## Open User Requests`, #81 v2) is judgment-only (AC9: the summarizer LLM judges openness), and the ledger's `kind=='user'` exempt tag only binds the JUDGE — the relief's keep-N hide, the checkpoint foldable range, and the local trim valve all folded delivered mail like noise. The channel delivery shape (`from <id> in #<channel>:`) additionally escapes the DM-only `_agentMailPattern` in `isSyntheticUserText`.\n\n**The belt (`compaction/inbound_mail.dart`).** One record- and message-level definition consumed by all tiers:\n- `isAgentMailText` (user_text.dart): DM shape, channel shape, reply anchor;\n- a mail record with no later reply never enters the engine's foldable range, never passes `validateHidePicks` (pinned), never joins the relief's keep-N veto (passes 1/2), and the trim valve CARRIES it across the cut like the pinned newest user turn;\n- reply evidence is deliberately conservative: an `agent_message` tool call or pure prose closes the mail; ordinary tool-call carriers are the agent working, not answering (the naive any-assistant rule made the invariant dead code in agentic sessions — caught by the tests before it shipped);\n- answered mail folds like any other data (protection stays bounded).\n\n**Scope decision.** Channel mail intentionally stays OUT of `isSyntheticUserText` — flipping it changes newest-real-user-turn semantics far beyond this belt (obligations ledger, checkpoint auto-close, gh-241 pin tests). The unanswered-mail invariant is the targeted fix.\n\n**Validation.** 16 new tests (`inbound_mail_test.dart`): text shapes, record/message matrices, validateHidePicks pins incl. the judge-exempt regression guard, valve carry/drop, relief end-to-end (fixture geometry pinned: transcript > relief target, newest result inside the valve's keep budget, so the carried path actually runs). Full `test/compaction/` + `auto_compactor`: 955 green; analyze clean.\n\nAlso captured in this thread: live validation runs of the PR's compaction stack on a copy of a real 544 KB DAP session — manual `/compact` (judge call to glm-5.3-flash, honest empty-range hand-over) and a fully AUTO `structured·hand-over` pass at cap 34000 (82 records hidden, 29848→18642 tokens, −38%, durable checkpoint with identities/agreements/verbatim errors preserved)."
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "rootCommentId": null,
      "threadId": null,
      "path": null,
      "line": null,
      "resolved": false,
      "bot": false,
      "body": "**Addendum 2 (owner directive): `dec76c67d6` — the chain token budget is OFF by default.**\n\nThe clip that motivated the mail-compaction belt also exposed the #2226 budget pause as a wake-gate that fires AFTER the spend: the evidence line showed 34.8M tokens booked across one marathon run, with the pause landing on the next wake and the peer's mail queued behind it. Per the owner's directive (\"let the mail arrive\"), `messaging.chainBudgetTokens` now defaults to **0**: spend alone never pauses a chain. The loop detector (content-similarity + no-progress evidence) stays ON as the default bound for true storms; a positive `messaging.chainBudgetTokens` re-enables the #2226 pause verbatim (400000 was the pre-#2435 default).\n\nTests: config defaults pin cap OFF + detection ON + budget OFF; the bare-policy guard never budget-pauses after a 50M-token marathon spend; the explicit-positive parse is unchanged. messaging (185) + cli inbox-wake suites green; analyze clean."
